      <data key="d2">Generation of Amadori products is the major single modification by the Maillard reaction in vivo and a source of biologically active glycoxidation products leading to protein cross-linking in biological tissues. Amadoriases are FAD enzymes which catalyze the oxidative deglycation of Amadori products into deoxyglucosone, hydrogen peroxide, and the corresponding primary amine (PubMed:18667417, PubMed:19888573, PubMed:20383736, PubMed:21755947, PubMed:9139700). The substrate is oxidized by the flavin in the reductive half-reaction, and the reduced flavin is then oxidized by molecular oxygen in the oxidative half-reaction (PubMed:20383736, PubMed:21755947)</data>
