    <node id="protein:Q12965">
      <data key="d0">PROTEIN</data>
      <data key="d1">Unconventional myosin-Ie</data>
      <data key="d2">Actin-based motor molecule with ATPase activity (PubMed:11940582, PubMed:36316095). Unconventional myosins serve in intracellular movements. Their highly divergent tails bind to membranous compartments, which are then moved relative to actin filaments. Binds to membranes containing anionic phospholipids via its tail domain. Involved in clathrin-mediated endocytosis and intracellular movement of clathrin-coated vesicles (PubMed:36316095). Required for normal morphology of the glomerular basement membrane, normal development of foot processes by kidney podocytes and normal kidney function. In dendritic cells, may control the movement of class II-containing cytoplasmic vesicles along the actin cytoskeleton by connecting them with the actin network via ARL14EP and ARL14</data>
      <data key="d3">1.0</data>
      <data key="d4">UniProt:Q12965</data>
      <data key="d7">Homo sapiens</data>
