    <node id="protein:G2WRE6">
      <data key="d0">PROTEIN</data>
      <data key="d1">Secreted metalloproteases M35-1</data>
      <data key="d2">Secreted metalloproteinase that triggers the burst of reactive oxygen species (ROS) in host plant cells leading to cell death (PubMed:36222688). M35-1-induced cell death in Nicotiana benthamiana depends on BAK1 and SOBIR1 (PubMed:36222688). Also essential for normal vegetative growth and conidial production, and participates in stress adaptation (PubMed:36222688). Positively regulated pathogenicity but is not involved in mycellium penetration (PubMed:36222688)</data>
      <data key="d3">1.0</data>
      <data key="d4">UniProt:G2WRE6</data>
      <data key="d7">Verticillium dahliae (strain VdLs.17 / ATCC MYA-4575 / FGSC 10137)</data>
      <data key="d20">3.4.24.39</data>
      <data key="d21">M35-1</data>
      <data key="d22" />
      <data key="d23">355</data>
      <data key="d24">True</data>
    </node>
    <node id="protein:G2X2M7">
      <data key="d0">PROTEIN</data>
      <data key="d1">Secreted metalloproteases ASPF2</data>
      <data key="d2">Secreted metalloproteinase that triggers the burst of reactive oxygen species (ROS) in host plant cells leading to cell death (PubMed:36222688). ASPF2 induced cell death in Nicotiana benthamiana does not depend on BAK1 and SOBIR1 (PubMed:36222688). Competes with Arabidopsis MYB6 for binding to E3 ligases plant U-box 25 (PUB25) and PUB26. MYB6 promotes plant resistance to Verticillium wilt while PUBs ubiquitinate MYB6 and mediate its degradation (PubMed:34469582). Also essential for normal vegetative growth and conidial production, and participates in stress adaptation (PubMed:28291379, PubMed:36222688). Required for the expression of VDH1 and VMK1, two genes involved in microsclerotial formation (PubMed:28291379). Positively regulated pathogenicity but is not involved in mycellium penetration (PubMed:28291379, PubMed:36222688)</data>
      <data key="d3">1.0</data>
      <data key="d4">UniProt:G2X2M7</data>
      <data key="d7">Verticillium dahliae (strain VdLs.17 / ATCC MYA-4575 / FGSC 10137)</data>
